# Build-context allowlist for mcp-server/Dockerfile.
#
# Everything is excluded, then only what the image build needs is re-included.
# An allowlist rather than a denylist on purpose: a stray local file in this
# directory (a scratch script, a local .env, an editor backup) must never land
# in an image layer, and a denylist only covers the names someone thought of.
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` runs after `npm ci` and copies the host's
# node_modules/ over the freshly installed one, plus dist/, the test harnesses
# and any untracked file, into the image.
#
# The image needs: the manifests (npm ci), tsconfig.json + src/ (npm run build).
# dist/ is rebuilt inside the image, so the host copy is excluded too — a stale
# host dist/ file with no matching src/ file would otherwise survive the build.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!src
